{"type":"message","id":"f36896eb","parentId":"157ab2b2","timestamp":"2026-02-18T13:16:58.651Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm clearly getting no output at all from any command. This is suspicious. Perhaps the OpenClaw runtime has restrictions on executing Windows commands, or the exec tool is misconfigured. Let me check the available tools again in my session context.\n\nLooking at my subagent context: I'm a subagent spawned by the main agent for a specific task. The task is to investigate the gateway restart flicker. My rules say: \"You are NOT the main agent. Don't try to be.\" and \"Do not initiate\" but I can use tools.\n\nMaybe I should try using the `message` tool to communicate with the main agent? But that's for external messages, not for reporting back. My final response will be automatically reported to the main agent, so I don't need to use message.\n\nGiven that I cannot seem to get any command output, I might need to approach this differently. Perhaps I can look at the file system for configuration files related to OpenClaw.\n\nLet me try to check the OpenClaw state directory, which is: D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\.openclaw-state\\workspace-coder2\n\nThat's my workspace. Maybe there are logs or config files there that can help.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_36e12f3a01b047cdb2ac3d11","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\.openclaw-state\\workspace-coder2"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":13526,"output":589,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":14115,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771420615439}}
