{"type":"message","id":"c3e3b5d9","parentId":"cedc8adf","timestamp":"2026-02-18T13:23:50.773Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting! The CommandLine appears to be incomplete. It only shows the powershell path with no arguments. That suggests the process might be a PowerShell that was started without extra arguments? But we saw the window title \"openclaw-tui\". That title could have been set by the script running inside PowerShell. So the actual command might just be `powershell.exe` and then the script sets the title. So the command line may not have the -File argument if the script was invoked via other means (maybe via a shortcut that runs a command which sets the title and then runs something).\n\nMaybe it's a `start` command with a title? Like `start \"openclaw-tui\" powershell ...`? Or maybe it's a script that does `$host.ui.RawUI.WindowTitle = \"openclaw-tui\"`.\n\nI should look for any batch files or shortcuts that might launch openclaw-tui. Let me search for the string \"openclaw-tui\" on the system.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_608b6722a44942c6b3a0f2c8","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"powershell -NoProfile -Command \"Get-ChildItem -Path D:\\ -Recurse -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Where-Object { $_.Name -like '*openclaw*' -or $_.Name -like '*tui*' } | Select-Object FullName, Length | Format-Table -AutoSize\"","pty":true,"timeout":120}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":92999,"output":547,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":93546,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771421023433}}
