{"type":"message","id":"a5e44764","parentId":"606001f6","timestamp":"2026-02-18T13:25:36.773Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting! The parent process is explorer.exe, with no command line arguments from the parent (that's normal, explorer is the shell). The child process (22972) has CommandLine: `\"C:\\Windows\\System32\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\powershell.exe\"` (just the basic, no -File or -Command). That suggests that the PowerShell was started with an interactive shell, maybe via a shortcut that sets the window title and then runs a profile script or something.\n\nSince the CommandLine doesn't include a script, it might be that the user started it manually, or a shortcut that runs `powershell.exe` and then the title is set by a profile script or by the openclaw TUI itself. But the parent is explorer.exe, meaning it was launched from the desktop/start menu or file system. Could be from a shortcut. Let's check if there's a shortcut on the desktop or start menu that points to openclaw.\n\nSearch for shortcuts with \"openclaw\" in the name in the startup and desktop.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_2dadcadf333d4faaac35c7cb","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"powershell -NoProfile -Command \"$paths = @(\\\"$env:USERPROFILE\\Desktop\\\",\\\"$env:APPDATA\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Start Menu\\Programs\\\"); foreach ($p in $paths) { if (Test-Path $p) { Get-ChildItem -Path $p -Filter *.lnk -Recurse | Where-Object { $_.Name -like '*openclaw*' } | Select-Object FullName, Name } }\"","pty":true,"timeout":30}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":103796,"output":605,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":104401,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771421128203}}
