{"type":"message","id":"cd4f0a42","parentId":"7310da64","timestamp":"2026-02-18T13:26:37.642Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No matches. So there is no scheduled task that explicitly runs that batch file or the openclaw command. However, the user reports a recurring console window flicker (gateway restart loop). That could be caused by the gateway crashing repeatedly, and maybe something is monitoring it and restarting it. The batch file itself kills node processes and launches a new one. But what would trigger the batch file to run again?\n\nOne possibility: The shortcut on the desktop might be clicked repeatedly, but that's manual. Another possibility: There's a startup entry that runs the batch file. Let's check the startup folder and registry again for entries that point to that batch file or to openclaw.cmd.\n\nWe already saw the startup folder entries: Comet.lnk, desktop.ini, Send to OneNote.lnk, ShareX.lnk. None appear to be OpenClaw. But maybe there is an entry in the registry Run keys that we missed because we only listed them and didn't look for openclaw. Let's search the registry values for \"openclaw\" or \"clawdbot\".","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"Let's search the registry Run keys for entries related to OpenClaw:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_ac022f2dd28c464096f5dfe2","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"$regPaths = @(\n    \"HKLM:\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run\",\n    \"HKLM:\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\RunOnce\",\n    \"HKLM:\\Software\\Wow6432Node\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run\",\n    \"HKLM:\\Software\\Wow6432Node\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\RunOnce\",\n    \"HKCU:\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run\",\n    \"HKCU:\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\RunOnce\"\n)\nforeach ($regPath in $regPaths) {\n    if (Test-Path $regPath) {\n        try {\n            $props = Get-ItemProperty -Path $regPath -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue\n            if ($props) {\n                foreach ($prop in $props.PSObject.Properties) {\n                    if ($prop.Name -notmatch \"^(PSPath|PSParentPath|PSChildName|PSDrive|PSProvider)$\") {\n                        $value = $prop.Value\n                        if ($value -match 'openclaw|clawdbot|launch_openclaw|gateway|18789') {\n                            [PSCustomObject]@{\n                                RegistryPath = $regPath\n                                Name = $prop.Name\n                                Value = $value\n                            } | Format-List\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        } catch { }\n    }\n}\n","file_path":"D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\.openclaw-state\\workspace-coder2\\search_registry_run.ps1"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":106171,"output":860,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":107031,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771421181509}}
