{"type":"message","id":"db71f2cd","parentId":"1af3ac3f","timestamp":"2026-02-18T13:26:48.508Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No output. So no registry Run entries contain openclaw/clawdbot. So the shortcut is not in startup. Then what causes the gateway to restart repeatedly? Maybe the gateway itself has a built-in watchdog that restarts it if it crashes? Or maybe the `run-node.mjs` script has a loop that restarts the gateway if it exits? Let's inspect that file.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"Let's examine the launch script deeper: `scripts/run-node.mjs` in the clawdbot project:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_a1453ffe3cee42b9a859db06","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"D:\\workspace\\appDev\\clawdbot\\clawdbot\\scripts\\run-node.mjs"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":106970,"output":236,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":107206,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771421205383}}
{"type":"message","id":"5d7b59eb","parentId":"db71f2cd","timestamp":"2026-02-18T13:26:48.541Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_a1453ffe3cee42b9a859db06","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"#!/usr/bin/env node\nimport { spawn } from \"node:child_process\";\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\nimport process from \"node:process\";\n\nconst args = process.argv.slice(2);\nconst env = { ...process.env };\nconst cwd = process.cwd();\nconst compilerOverride = env.OPENCLAW_TS_COMPILER ?? env.CLAWDBOT_TS_COMPILER;\nconst compiler = compilerOverride === \"tsc\" ? \"tsc\" : \"tsgo\";\nconst projectArgs = [\"--project\", \"tsconfig.json\"];\n\nconst distRoot = path.join(cwd, \"dist\");\nconst distEntry = path.join(distRoot, \"/entry.js\");\nconst buildStampPath = path.join(distRoot, \".buildstamp\");\nconst srcRoot = path.join(cwd, \"src\");\nconst configFiles = [path.join(cwd, \"tsconfig.json\"), path.join(cwd, \"package.json\")];\n\nconst statMtime = (filePath) => {\n  try {\n    return fs.statSync(filePath).mtimeMs;\n  } catch {\n    return null;\n  }\n};\n\nconst isExcludedSource = (filePath) => {\n  const relativePath = path.relative(srcRoot, filePath);\n  if (relativePath.startsWith(\"..\")) return false;\n  return (\n    relativePath.endsWith(\".test.ts\") ||\n    relativePath.endsWith(\".test.tsx\") ||\n    relativePath.endsWith(`test-helpers.ts`)\n  );\n};\n\nconst findLatestMtime = (dirPath, shouldSkip) => {\n  let latest = null;\n  const queue = [dirPath];\n  while (queue.length > 0) {\n    const current = queue.pop();\n    if (!current) continue;\n    let entries = [];\n    try {\n      entries = fs.readdirSync(current, { withFileTypes: true });\n    } catch {\n      continue;\n    }\n    for (const entry of entries) {\n      const fullPath = path.join(current, entry.name);\n      if (entry.isDirectory()) {\n        queue.push(fullPath);\n        continue;\n      }\n      if (!entry.isFile()) continue;\n      if (shouldSkip?.(fullPath)) continue;\n      const mtime = statMtime(fullPath);\n      if (mtime == null) continue;\n      if (latest == null || mtime > latest) {\n        latest = mtime;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  return latest;\n};\n\nconst shouldBuild = () => {\n  if (env.OPENCLAW_FORCE_BUILD === \"1\") return true;\n  const stampMtime = statMtime(buildStampPath);\n  if (stampMtime == null) return true;\n  if (statMtime(distEntry) == null) return true;\n\n  for (const filePath of configFiles) {\n    const mtime = statMtime(filePath);\n    if (mtime != null && mtime > stampMtime) return true;\n  }\n\n  const srcMtime = findLatestMtime(srcRoot, isExcludedSource);\n  if (srcMtime != null && srcMtime > stampMtime) return true;\n  return false;\n};\n\nconst logRunner = (message) => {\n  if (env.OPENCLAW_RUNNER_LOG === \"0\") return;\n  process.stderr.write(`[openclaw] ${message}\\n`);\n};\n\nconst runNode = () => {\n  const nodeProcess = spawn(process.execPath, [\"openclaw.mjs\", ...args], {\n    cwd,\n    env,\n    stdio: \"inherit\",\n  });\n\n  nodeProcess.on(\"exit\", (exitCode, exitSignal) => {\n    if (exitSignal) {\n      process.exit(1);\n    }\n    process.exit(exitCode ?? 1);\n  });\n};\n\nconst writeBuildStamp = () => {\n  try {\n    fs.mkdirSync(distRoot, { recursive: true });\n    fs.writeFileSync(buildStampPath, `${Date.now()}\\n`);\n  } catch (error) {\n    // Best-effort stamp; still allow the runner to start.\n    logRunner(`Failed to write build stamp: ${error?.message ?? \"unknown error\"}`);\n  }\n};\n\nif (!shouldBuild()) {\n  runNode();\n} else {\n  logRunner(\"Building TypeScript (dist is stale).\");\n  const pnpmArgs = [\"exec\", compiler, ...projectArgs];\n  const buildCmd = process.platform === \"win32\" ? \"cmd.exe\" : \"pnpm\";\n  const buildArgs =\n    process.platform === \"win32\" ? [\"/d\", \"/s\", \"/c\", \"pnpm\", ...pnpmArgs] : pnpmArgs;\n  const build = spawn(buildCmd, buildArgs, {\n    cwd,\n    env,\n    stdio: \"inherit\",\n  });\n\n  build.on(\"exit\", (code, signal) => {\n    if (signal) {\n      process.exit(1);\n    }\n    if (code !== 0 && code !== null) {\n      process.exit(code);\n    }\n    writeBuildStamp();\n    runNode();\n  });\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1771421208539}}
{"type":"message","id":"ff97f096","parentId":"5d7b59eb","timestamp":"2026-02-18T13:26:53.750Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This script (`run-node.mjs`) is a runner that:\n- Checks if a build is needed (if dist is stale)\n- If build needed, runs TypeScript compiler (tsc or tsgo) to build, then writes a build stamp and runs the node process with `openclaw.mjs`.\n- If no build needed, directly runs `openclaw.mjs` with the provided args (in this case \"gateway --port 18789 --allow-unconfigured\").\n\nThe runner does NOT have any automatic restart loop. It runs the node process once, and when that process exits, the runner exits. So the gateway TUI should not automatically restart unless something else restarts the batch file.\n\nNow, what could cause the batch file to be launched repeatedly? Possibly:\n- The gateway TUI itself might be a UI that you interact with, and it might have an option to restart, but that's manual.\n- There could be a scheduled task that runs the batch file at a certain interval (we didn't find any).\n- There could be a watchdog script that monitors the gateway and restarts it if it crashes. But we haven't found any such script.\n\nMaybe the flickering is not due to restarts but due to the TUI itself rapidly updating (like a console UI that refreshes). But the user said \"gateway restart loop\", implying it's crashing and restarting.\n\nLet's check the config-audit.jsonl log that was open in Notepad++. That might give clues. The script found Notepad++ with that file open. It's in the logs directory: `D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\.openclaw-state\\logs\\config-audit.jsonl`. Let's read it.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"Let's check the config audit log to see if there are errors:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_e15ca5e16ab04e16846f8cb6","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\.openclaw-state\\logs\\config-audit.jsonl","limit":50}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":108220,"output":815,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":109035,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771421208541}}
